Without a specific code example of what you are doing, I assume that 
this is:

print(fit).

There were substantial changes in rpy2-2.1 about that.
R is using a console output, so it felt more consistent to use the 
console callback (and somehow make all this more programmer-friendly).
I hoped to leave the win32 part intact, although without testing it and 
with the intent of getting the callbacks to finally work under win32 
(win32 is currently not officially supported for rpy2-2.1).





